doc:sch-2-sec-8-2-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "8(5) Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) This section applies to a function or power of an agency whether or not the agency has the function or power under an enactment. Note 1: See section 8C for restrictions on the requirement to publish this information. Note 2: The agency must have regard to the objects of this Act and guidelines issued by the Information Commissioner in performing functions, and exercising powers, under this section (see section 9A)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-2-sec-8a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8A Information to be published—what is operational information?"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-8a ;
    values:originalText "(1) An agency’s operational information is information held by the agency to assist the agency to perform or exercise the agency’s functions or powers in making decisions or recommendations affecting members of the public (or any particular person or entity, or class of persons or entities). Example: The agency’s rules, guidelines, practices and precedents relating to those decisions and recommendations.  (2) An agency’s operational information does not include information that is available to members of the public otherwise than by being published by (or on behalf of) the agency. 8B  Information to be published—accuracy etc.  An agency must ensure that information published by the agency as required or permitted by this Part is accurate, up-to-date and complete." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An agency’s operational information is information held by the agency to assist the agency to perform or exercise the agency’s functions or powers in making decisions or recommendations affecting members of the public (or any particular person or entity, or class of persons or entities). Example: The agency’s rules, guidelines, practices and precedents relating to those decisions and recommendations.  (2) An agency’s operational information does not include information that is available to members of the public otherwise than by being published by (or on behalf of) the agency. 8B  Information to be published—accuracy etc.  An agency must ensure that information published by the agency as required or permitted by this Part is accurate, up-to-date and complete."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b9e438a60207f6b61996805d29b21ac11cb706e79d7285c9e406a71aed4e2634" ;
    cof:pageNumber "13"^^xsd:integer ;
