doc:sch-3-sec-20-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20(5) Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) The agency or Minister must give the person access to the document if it is conditionally exempt at a particular time unless (in the circumstances) access to the document at that time would, on balance, be contrary to the public interest. Note 1: Division 3 of Part IV provides for when a document is conditionally exempt. Note 2: A conditionally exempt document is an exempt document if access to the document would, on balance, be contrary to the public interest (see section 31B (exempt documents for the purposes of Part IV)). Note 3: Section 11B deals with when it is contrary to the public interest to give a person access to the document." ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-20-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20(6) Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-20-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) Despite subsection (5), the agency or Minister is not required to give access to the document at a particular time if, at that time, the document is both:  (a) a conditionally exempt document; and  (b) an exempt document:  (i) under Division 2 of Part IV (exemptions); or  (ii) within the meaning of paragraph (b) or (c) of the definition of exempt document in subsection 4(1)." ;
    skos:definition "(6) Despite subsection (5), the agency or Minister is not required to give access to the document at a particular time if, at that time, the document is both:  (a) a conditionally exempt document; and  (b) an exempt document:  (i) under Division 2 of Part IV (exemptions); or  (ii) within the meaning of paragraph (b) or (c) of the definition of exempt document in subsection 4(1)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c2a10effb7abeaa46639526d5948dc6f51eca182f1f6b407cf6dc3fe9e1d3461" ;
