concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-22-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "22 Access to edited copies with exempt or irrelevant matter deleted"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-22-2 ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This section applies if:  (a) an agency or Minister decides:  (i) to refuse to give access to an exempt document; or  (ii) that to give access to a document would disclose information that would reasonably be regarded as irrelevant to the request for access; and  (b) it is possible for the agency or Minister to prepare a copy (an edited copy) of the document, modified by deletions, ensuring that:  (i) access to the edited copy would be required to be given under section 11A (access to documents on request); and  (ii) the edited copy would not disclose any information that would reasonably be regarded as irrelevant to the request; and  (c) it is reasonably practicable for the agency or Minister to prepare the edited copy, having regard to:  (i) the nature and extent of the modification; and  (ii) the resources available to modify the document; and  (d) it is not apparent (from the request or from consultation with the applicant) that the applicant would decline access to the edited copy. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 3  Exemptions" ;
    skos:definition "Scope  (1) This section applies if:  (a) an agency or Minister decides:  (i) to refuse to give access to an exempt document; or  (ii) that to give access to a document would disclose information that would reasonably be regarded as irrelevant to the request for access; and  (b) it is possible for the agency or Minister to prepare a copy (an edited copy) of the document, modified by deletions, ensuring that:  (i) access to the edited copy would be required to be given under section 11A (access to documents on request); and  (ii) the edited copy would not disclose any information that would reasonably be regarded as irrelevant to the request; and  (c) it is reasonably practicable for the agency or Minister to prepare the edited copy, having regard to:  (i) the nature and extent of the modification; and  (ii) the resources available to modify the document; and  (d) it is not apparent (from the request or from consultation with the applicant) that the applicant would decline access to the edited copy. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 3  Exemptions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "682fbbc54be8ff8b9d0779da67723ebbac76056ce538c08c65dfdf239baa395c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "27"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Agency or Minister may prepare edited copy of document for access under section 11A." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf, p.27" ;
    cml:asserts concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-22-2-norm .
