doc:sch-3-sec-26a-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "26A(3) Consultation—documents affecting Commonwealth-State" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If, after such consultation has taken place, the agency or Minister decides to give the applicant access to the document, the agency or Minister must give written notice of the decision to both of the following:  (a) the State;  (b) the applicant. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 3  Exemptions" ;
    cof:pageNumber "29"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-26 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26 Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-26 ;
    values:originalText "Access not to be given until review or appeal opportunities have run out  (4) However, the agency or Minister must not give the applicant access to the document unless, after all the opportunities of the State for review or appeal in relation to the decision to give access to the document have run out, the decision still stands, or is confirmed. Note 1: The decision to give access to the document is subject to internal review (see Part VI), review by the Information Commissioner (see" ;
    skos:definition "Access not to be given until review or appeal opportunities have run out  (4) However, the agency or Minister must not give the applicant access to the document unless, after all the opportunities of the State for review or appeal in relation to the decision to give access to the document have run out, the decision still stands, or is confirmed. Note 1: The decision to give access to the document is subject to internal review (see Part VI), review by the Information Commissioner (see"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4d02ef46f6a10830e870dcc808e3230a8e7ced6190946ada2c4379efb716db19" ;
