doc:sch-3-sec-32 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "32 Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "How this Act applies to exempt and conditionally exempt documents Item If … then … because of … access to a document is refused because it contains exempt matter, and the exempt matter can be deleted (a) an edited copy deleting the exempt matter must be prepared (if practicable); and (b) access to the edited copy must be given; section 22. a document is an exempt document because of any provision of this Act access to the document may be given apart from under this Act section 3A (objects— information or documents otherwise accessible)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-31b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31B Exempt documents for the purposes of this Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-31b ;
    values:originalText "A document is exempt for the purposes of this Part if:  (a) it is an exempt document under Division 2; or  (b) it is conditionally exempt under Division 3, and access to the document would, on balance, be contrary to the public interest for the purposes of subsection 11A(5). Note 1: A document is an exempt document for the purposes of this Act (see subsection 4(1)) if: (a) it is exempt under this section; or (b) it is exempt because of section 7 (exemption of certain persons and bodies); or (c) it is an official document of a Minister that contains matters not relating to the affairs of an agency or a Department of State. Note 2: Access must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A)." ;
    skos:definition "A document is exempt for the purposes of this Part if:  (a) it is an exempt document under Division 2; or  (b) it is conditionally exempt under Division 3, and access to the document would, on balance, be contrary to the public interest for the purposes of subsection 11A(5). Note 1: A document is an exempt document for the purposes of this Act (see subsection 4(1)) if: (a) it is exempt under this section; or (b) it is exempt because of section 7 (exemption of certain persons and bodies); or (c) it is an official document of a Minister that contains matters not relating to the affairs of an agency or a Department of State. Note 2: Access must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "068ec85f443be5a4c473c19d7f3dc316114bada5036dd04e4a2c4ccaebaf40d4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A document is exempt if it meets certain conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf, p.36" ;
    cml:asserts concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-31b-norm .
