concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-34 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "34 Cabinet documents"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-34 ;
    values:originalText "General rules  (1) A document is an exempt document if:  (a) both of the following are satisfied:  (i) it has been submitted to the Cabinet for its consideration, or is or was proposed by a Minister to be so submitted;  (ii) it was brought into existence for the dominant purpose of submission for consideration by the Cabinet; or  (b) it is an official record of the Cabinet; or  (c) it was brought into existence for the dominant purpose of briefing a Minister on a document to which paragraph (a) applies; or  (d) it is a draft of a document to which paragraph (a), (b) or (c) applies.  (2) A document is an exempt document to the extent that it is a copy or part of, or contains an extract from, a document to which subsection (1) applies.  (3) A document is an exempt document to the extent that it contains information the disclosure of which would reveal a Cabinet deliberation or decision, unless the existence of the deliberation or decision has been officially disclosed. Exceptions  (4) A document is not an exempt document only because it is attached to a document to which subsection (1), (2) or (3) applies. Note: However, the attachment itself may be an exempt document. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 3  Exemptions" ;
    skos:definition "General rules  (1) A document is an exempt document if:  (a) both of the following are satisfied:  (i) it has been submitted to the Cabinet for its consideration, or is or was proposed by a Minister to be so submitted;  (ii) it was brought into existence for the dominant purpose of submission for consideration by the Cabinet; or  (b) it is an official record of the Cabinet; or  (c) it was brought into existence for the dominant purpose of briefing a Minister on a document to which paragraph (a) applies; or  (d) it is a draft of a document to which paragraph (a), (b) or (c) applies.  (2) A document is an exempt document to the extent that it is a copy or part of, or contains an extract from, a document to which subsection (1) applies.  (3) A document is an exempt document to the extent that it contains information the disclosure of which would reveal a Cabinet deliberation or decision, unless the existence of the deliberation or decision has been officially disclosed. Exceptions  (4) A document is not an exempt document only because it is attached to a document to which subsection (1), (2) or (3) applies. Note: However, the attachment itself may be an exempt document. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 3  Exemptions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3eeec05e3dd48aadf8f659c8b76b660eccb3fb8ec9615e6dcfba39d8a58858a8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "37"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-34-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-34-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-34-ss-3 ;
