doc:sch-3-sec-47d a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "47D Public interest conditional exemptions—financial or property" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "interests of the Commonwealth  A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act would have a substantial adverse effect on the financial or property interests of the Commonwealth or of an agency. Note: Access must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "41"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-47e a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "47E Public interest conditional exemptions—certain operations of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-47e ;
    values:originalText "agencies  A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act would, or could reasonably be expected to, do any of the following:  (a) prejudice the effectiveness of procedures or methods for the conduct of tests, examinations or audits by an agency;  (b) prejudice the attainment of the objects of particular tests, examinations or audits conducted or to be conducted by an agency;  (c) have a substantial adverse effect on the management or assessment of personnel by the Commonwealth or by an agency;  (d) have a substantial adverse effect on the proper and efficient conduct of the operations of an agency. Note: Access must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 3  Exemptions" ;
    skos:definition "agencies  A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act would, or could reasonably be expected to, do any of the following:  (a) prejudice the effectiveness of procedures or methods for the conduct of tests, examinations or audits by an agency;  (b) prejudice the attainment of the objects of particular tests, examinations or audits conducted or to be conducted by an agency;  (c) have a substantial adverse effect on the management or assessment of personnel by the Commonwealth or by an agency;  (d) have a substantial adverse effect on the proper and efficient conduct of the operations of an agency. Note: Access must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 3  Exemptions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5dd4d1d9573fca3189d3e6ea73b692c4af5a85067b33898114c53c5ed31ee533" ;
