concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-47h a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "47H Public interest conditional exemptions—research"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-47h ;
    values:originalText "A document is conditionally exempt if:  (a) it contains information relating to research that is being, or is to be, undertaken by an officer of an agency specified in Schedule 4; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Exemptions  Schedule 3 Main exemption amendments  Part 2  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          41  (b) disclosure of the information before the completion of the research would be likely unreasonably to expose the agency or officer to disadvantage. Note: Access must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A)." ;
    skos:definition "A document is conditionally exempt if:  (a) it contains information relating to research that is being, or is to be, undertaken by an officer of an agency specified in Schedule 4; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Exemptions  Schedule 3 Main exemption amendments  Part 2  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          41  (b) disclosure of the information before the completion of the research would be likely unreasonably to expose the agency or officer to disadvantage. Note: Access must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ef7b0a8b54b2775d50decdbb3905979fefc0cd0ff8724e710de1c7d9c1fc5afb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "44"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Conditional exemptions for research documents" ;
