concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-31 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31 Decision to impose charge—extended period for processing"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-31 ;
    values:originalText "request Scope  (1) This section applies if:  (a) on a particular day (the charge notice day) an applicant in relation to a request receives a notice under subsection 29(1) or (6) to the effect that the applicant is liable to pay a charge in respect of the request; and  (b) the notice is received before the end of the period (the processing period) applicable under paragraph 15(5)(b) in relation to the request (or that period as extended). Processing period to be calculated disregarding period when charge unpaid  (2) In working out the length of the processing period (or that period as extended) for the purposes of paragraph 15(5)(b), disregard the number of days in the period starting on the charge notice day and ending on the earliest occurring of the following days:  (a) the day the applicant pays the amount of the charge (or a deposit on account of the charge prescribed by the ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments" ;
    skos:definition "request Scope  (1) This section applies if:  (a) on a particular day (the charge notice day) an applicant in relation to a request receives a notice under subsection 29(1) or (6) to the effect that the applicant is liable to pay a charge in respect of the request; and  (b) the notice is received before the end of the period (the processing period) applicable under paragraph 15(5)(b) in relation to the request (or that period as extended). Processing period to be calculated disregarding period when charge unpaid  (2) In working out the length of the processing period (or that period as extended) for the purposes of paragraph 15(5)(b), disregard the number of days in the period starting on the charge notice day and ending on the earliest occurring of the following days:  (a) the day the applicant pays the amount of the charge (or a deposit on account of the charge prescribed by the ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0b5f8b98229081140aa6483acc2a5e616cbf97954270f3e11a60954976b5a05f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "53"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-31-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-31-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf, p.53" .
doc:sch-4-sec-31 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "31 Decision to impose charge—extended period for processing" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "request Scope  (1) This section applies if:  (a) on a particular day (the charge notice day) an applicant in relation to a request receives a notice under subsection 29(1) or (6) to the effect that the applicant is liable to pay a charge in respect of the request; and  (b) the notice is received before the end of the period (the processing period) applicable under paragraph 15(5)(b) in relation to the request (or that period as extended). Processing period to be calculated disregarding period when charge unpaid  (2) In working out the length of the processing period (or that period as extended) for the purposes of paragraph 15(5)(b), disregard the number of days in the period starting on the charge notice day and ending on the earliest occurring of the following days:  (a) the day the applicant pays the amount of the charge (or a deposit on account of the charge prescribed by the ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments" ;
    cof:pageNumber "53"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-31-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
