doc:sch-4-sec-54 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "54 Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Access grant decisions Item If, in relation to a request for access to a document ... the access grant decision is ... section 27 (business documents) applies in relation to business information in the document a decision of an agency or Minister to give access to the document (or an edited copy of the document) because: (a) the document is neither exempt under section 47, nor conditionally exempt under section 47G; or (b) if the document is conditionally exempt under section 47G—access to the document would not, on balance, be contrary to the public interest for the purposes of subsection 11A(5). Note: Section 47 deals with documents disclosing trade secrets or commercially valuable information. Section 47G deals with other business documents. section 27A (documents affecting personal privacy) applies in relation to personal information in the document about a living person a decision of an agency or Minister to give the applicant access to the document (or an edited copy of the document) because: (a) the document is not conditionally exempt under section 47F (personal privacy); or (b) access to the document would not, on balance, be contrary to the public interest for the purposes of subsection 11A(5). section 27A (documents affecting personal privacy) applies in relation to personal information in the document about a deceased person a decision of an agency or Minister to give the applicant access to the document (or an edited copy of the document) because: (a) the document is not conditionally exempt under section 47F (personal privacy); or (b) access to the document would not, on balance, be contrary to the public interest for the purposes of subsection 11A(5). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          55" ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-53c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "53C Internal review—who is an affected third party?"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-53c ;
    values:originalText "The following table has effect:  Who is an affected third party? Item If, in relation to a request for access to a document ... the affected third party for the document is ... consultation with a State under section 26A (documents affecting Commonwealth-State relations) is required the State. section 27 (business documents) applies in relation to business information in the document the person or organisation concerned (within the meaning of section 27). section 27A (documents affecting personal privacy) applies in relation to personal information in the document about a living person the person. section 27A (documents affecting personal privacy) applies in relation to personal information in the document about a deceased person the legal personal representative of the deceased person." ;
    skos:definition "The following table has effect:  Who is an affected third party? Item If, in relation to a request for access to a document ... the affected third party for the document is ... consultation with a State under section 26A (documents affecting Commonwealth-State relations) is required the State. section 27 (business documents) applies in relation to business information in the document the person or organisation concerned (within the meaning of section 27). section 27A (documents affecting personal privacy) applies in relation to personal information in the document about a living person the person. section 27A (documents affecting personal privacy) applies in relation to personal information in the document about a deceased person the legal personal representative of the deceased person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d6ddb9e16558c918c6119fb40cc08f8c6ba6febc3ab7efcc78e59e831bc34be9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines who is an affected third party for a document request." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf, p.59" ;
    cml:asserts concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-53c-norm .
