    cof:title "54B(1) Internal review—application for review" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) An application for internal review must be in writing and must be made:  (a) within 30 days, or such further period as the agency allows, after the day the decision is notified to the applicant for internal review (the internal review applicant); or  (b) in the case of an access refusal decision of a kind mentioned in paragraph 53A(b), (c) or (f), within whichever of the following is the longer period:  (i) 30 days, or such further period as the agency allows, after the day the decision is notified to the internal review applicant;  (ii) 15 days after the day the access referred to in that paragraph was given (or purported to be given)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-54b-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "54B(2) Internal review—application for review"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-54b-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A decision by an agency to allow a further period for making an application may be made whether or not the time for making such an application has already expired." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A decision by an agency to allow a further period for making an application may be made whether or not the time for making such an application has already expired."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3dd54bfd4ca301de2fb1c94b0050037a3296309a4a00e60a15a6f39459651e00" ;
    values:partOf concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-54b ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Agency may extend application deadline" ;
