concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-54k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "54K Key concepts—what is an IC reviewable decision?"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-54k ;
    values:originalText "An IC reviewable decision is:  (a) a decision covered by subsection 54L(2) (access refusal decisions); or  (b) a decision covered by subsection 54M(2) (access grant decisions). Note: IC reviewable decision is short for Information Commissioner reviewable decision. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          61" ;
    skos:definition "An IC reviewable decision is:  (a) a decision covered by subsection 54L(2) (access refusal decisions); or  (b) a decision covered by subsection 54M(2) (access grant decisions). Note: IC reviewable decision is short for Information Commissioner reviewable decision. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          61"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f615f8339070b7b73c94e1150a5b5aa55695919417bca080daeb1afe177265ea" ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines what is an IC reviewable decision." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
