    cml:premiseText "the agency or Minister must make a decision under section 54W (decision not to review) or 55K (decision on review)" ;
    cml:conclusionText "The agency or Minister must make a decision under section 54W (decision not to review) or 55K (decision on review) in relation to the deemed decision" ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "0.5000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-4-sec-68 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "68 Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(b) a person makes an IC review application for review of the deemed decision; and  (c) the Information Commissioner has not made a decision under section 54W (decision not to review) or 55K (decision on review) in relation to the deemed decision; and  (d) subsection 15AC(7), 51DA(6) or 54D(6) applies in relation to a decision (the actual decision) made by the agency or Minister.  (2) The Information Commissioner must deal with the IC review application for review of the deemed decision as if it were an IC review application for the review of the actual decision, subject otherwise to this Part. Note: When making the actual decision, a consultation requirement under section 26A (documents affecting Commonwealth-State relations), 27 (business documents) or 27A (documents affecting personal privacy) may apply." ;
    cof:pageNumber "72"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-54z a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "54Z Procedure in IC review—general notice requirement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-54z ;
    values:originalText "Before undertaking an IC review, the Information Commissioner must inform:  (a) the person, agency or Minister who made the decision; or  (b) if the IC review application is made under section 54M (access grant decisions)—the person who made the request." ;
    skos:definition "Before undertaking an IC review, the Information Commissioner must inform:  (a) the person, agency or Minister who made the decision; or  (b) if the IC review application is made under section 54M (access grant decisions)—the person who made the request."@en ;
