concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-55g a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "55G Procedure in IC review—revocation or variation of access"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-55g ;
    values:originalText "refusal decision  (1) An agency or Minister may vary (or set aside and substitute) an access refusal decision (the original decision) in relation to a request or an application under section 48 at any time during an IC review of the access refusal decision if the variation or substitution (the revised decision) would have an effect of:  (a) giving access to a document in accordance with the request; or  (b) relieving the IC review applicant from liability to pay a charge; or  (c) requiring a record of personal information to be amended or annotated in accordance with the application. Note: When making the revised decision, a consultation requirement under section 26A (documents affecting Commonwealth-State relations), 27 (business documents) or 27A (documents affecting personal privacy) may apply.  (2) If an agency or Minister varies (or sets aside and substitutes) an access refusal decision under subsection (1): ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments" ;
    skos:definition "refusal decision  (1) An agency or Minister may vary (or set aside and substitute) an access refusal decision (the original decision) in relation to a request or an application under section 48 at any time during an IC review of the access refusal decision if the variation or substitution (the revised decision) would have an effect of:  (a) giving access to a document in accordance with the request; or  (b) relieving the IC review applicant from liability to pay a charge; or  (c) requiring a record of personal information to be amended or annotated in accordance with the application. Note: When making the revised decision, a consultation requirement under section 26A (documents affecting Commonwealth-State relations), 27 (business documents) or 27A (documents affecting personal privacy) may apply.  (2) If an agency or Minister varies (or sets aside and substitutes) an access refusal decision under subsection (1): ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "eb20867557663d552edf4f62fbe1b46ac60f98e6df0f040540c6e67d17af008e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "77"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-55g-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-55g-ss-2 ;
