    values:originalText "affirmation  (1) If, by a notice under subsection 55W(1), the Information Commissioner requires a person to appear before him or her, the Information Commissioner may:  (a) administer an oath or affirmation to the person; and  (b) examine the person on oath or affirmation.  (2) The oath or affirmation to be taken or made by a person for the purposes of this section is an oath or affirmation that the answers the person will give will be true. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          83  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is required under this section to be examined on oath or affirmation; and  (b) the person engages in conduct; and  (c) the person’s conduct breaches that requirement. Penalty for a contravention of this subsection: 6 months imprisonment. Note: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility." ;
    skos:definition "affirmation  (1) If, by a notice under subsection 55W(1), the Information Commissioner requires a person to appear before him or her, the Information Commissioner may:  (a) administer an oath or affirmation to the person; and  (b) examine the person on oath or affirmation.  (2) The oath or affirmation to be taken or made by a person for the purposes of this section is an oath or affirmation that the answers the person will give will be true. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          83  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is required under this section to be examined on oath or affirmation; and  (b) the person engages in conduct; and  (c) the person’s conduct breaches that requirement. Penalty for a contravention of this subsection: 6 months imprisonment. Note: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a69ad33c292fe18441e94306be54fc9a52e27fb2686932199c0b719fa2d803b2" ;
