doc:sch-4-sec-88-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "88(3) Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Subsection (2) does not limit the Federal Court of Australia’s power under subsection 56(6) to make an order remitting the case to be heard and decided again by the Information Commissioner." ;
    cof:pageNumber "92"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-57 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "57 Review by the Tribunal—guide"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-57 ;
    values:originalText "An application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for the review of certain decisions (see section 57A). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          89 Division 3 sets out the powers of the Tribunal in a review. Division 4 deals with the procedure to be followed in a review by the Tribunal. Division 5 deals with ensuring that exempt matter that comes before the Tribunal is protected from disclosure. Division 6 deals with the circumstances in which the Tribunal may make recommendations as to costs. Division 7 deals with the stay of decisions pending appeal to the Federal Court of Australia." ;
    skos:definition "An application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for the review of certain decisions (see section 57A). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          89 Division 3 sets out the powers of the Tribunal in a review. Division 4 deals with the procedure to be followed in a review by the Tribunal. Division 5 deals with ensuring that exempt matter that comes before the Tribunal is protected from disclosure. Division 6 deals with the circumstances in which the Tribunal may make recommendations as to costs. Division 7 deals with the stay of decisions pending appeal to the Federal Court of Australia."@en ;
