concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-61 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "61 Onus"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-61 ;
    values:originalText "(1) In proceedings under this Part for review of a decision in relation to a request, or in relation to an application under section 48 (a personal records application):  (a) if an agency or a Minister applied for the review—the agency or Minister has the onus of establishing that the decision is not justified, or that the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the applicant in relation to the request or the personal records application; or  (b) if the applicant in relation to the request or the personal records application applied for the review—the agency to ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments" ;
    skos:definition "(1) In proceedings under this Part for review of a decision in relation to a request, or in relation to an application under section 48 (a personal records application):  (a) if an agency or a Minister applied for the review—the agency or Minister has the onus of establishing that the decision is not justified, or that the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the applicant in relation to the request or the personal records application; or  (b) if the applicant in relation to the request or the personal records application applied for the review—the agency to ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments"@en ;
