concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-94 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "94 Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-94 ;
    values:originalText "which, or the Minister to whom, the request or personal records application was made has the onus of establishing that the decision is justified, or that the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the applicant.  (2) However, in proceedings under this Part that relate to a decision to give access to a document to which a consultation requirement applies under section 26A, 27 or 27A, an affected third party for the document in relation to which the decision was made has, if the affected third party is a party to the proceeding, the onus of establishing that:  (a) a decision refusing to give access to the document is justified; or  (b) the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the person who made the relevant request. Note: For affected third party, see section 53C." ;
    skos:definition "which, or the Minister to whom, the request or personal records application was made has the onus of establishing that the decision is justified, or that the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the applicant.  (2) However, in proceedings under this Part that relate to a decision to give access to a document to which a consultation requirement applies under section 26A, 27 or 27A, an affected third party for the document in relation to which the decision was made has, if the affected third party is a party to the proceeding, the onus of establishing that:  (a) a decision refusing to give access to the document is justified; or  (b) the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the person who made the relevant request. Note: For affected third party, see section 53C."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3bbb3cfbcf1dc5152f04aab55bda063cc36cdb62d483435aa62f05ada9e8145d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "98"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Requester has onus to establish justification for decision." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
