concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-75 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "75 Information Commissioner investigations—notice requirements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-75 ;
    values:originalText "Notice to respondent agency before commencing investigation  (1) Before beginning an investigation, the Information Commissioner must notify the respondent agency in writing. Notice of decision not to investigate, or not to continue to investigate  (2) Subsection (3) applies if the Information Commissioner decides:  (a) not to investigate, or not to continue to investigate, a complaint made under section 70; or  (b) not to continue an investigation commenced at the Information Commissioner’s initiative.  (3) The Information Commissioner must, as soon as practicable, notify the complainant (if any) and the respondent agency of the decision in writing.  (4) A notice under subsection (3) must state the reasons for the Information Commissioner’s decision. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments" ;
    skos:definition "Notice to respondent agency before commencing investigation  (1) Before beginning an investigation, the Information Commissioner must notify the respondent agency in writing. Notice of decision not to investigate, or not to continue to investigate  (2) Subsection (3) applies if the Information Commissioner decides:  (a) not to investigate, or not to continue to investigate, a complaint made under section 70; or  (b) not to continue an investigation commenced at the Information Commissioner’s initiative.  (3) The Information Commissioner must, as soon as practicable, notify the complainant (if any) and the respondent agency of the decision in writing.  (4) A notice under subsection (3) must state the reasons for the Information Commissioner’s decision. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5818d735dd1f77c7b7c7f2ecc3665d48b547d0a0872f4505de556dfe345842b3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "105"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-75-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-75-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-75-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-75-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf, p.105" .
doc:sch-4-sec-75 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "75 Information Commissioner investigations—notice requirements" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Notice to respondent agency before commencing investigation  (1) Before beginning an investigation, the Information Commissioner must notify the respondent agency in writing. Notice of decision not to investigate, or not to continue to investigate  (2) Subsection (3) applies if the Information Commissioner decides:  (a) not to investigate, or not to continue to investigate, a complaint made under section 70; or  (b) not to continue an investigation commenced at the Information Commissioner’s initiative.  (3) The Information Commissioner must, as soon as practicable, notify the complainant (if any) and the respondent agency of the decision in writing.  (4) A notice under subsection (3) must state the reasons for the Information Commissioner’s decision. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments" ;
    cof:pageNumber "105"^^xsd:integer .

