doc:sch-4-sec-89d-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "89D(3) Information Commissioner investigations—limitation on" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The Information Commissioner must not, in the document, recommend that an amendment be made to a record if he or she is satisfied of either of the following:  (a) the record is a record of a decision, under an enactment, by a court, tribunal, authority or person;  (b) the decision whether to amend the record involves the determination of a question that the person seeking amendment of the record is, or has been, entitled to have determined by the agency (on internal review), the Information Commissioner, a court or tribunal." ;
    cof:pageNumber "116"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-89e a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "89E Information Commissioner investigations—protection from"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-89e ;
    values:originalText "civil action  (1) Civil proceedings do not lie against a person in respect of loss, damage or injury of any kind suffered by another person because ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          113 the first-mentioned person complains about an action under section 70.  (2) Subsection (1) only applies if the complaint is made in good faith." ;
    skos:definition "civil action  (1) Civil proceedings do not lie against a person in respect of loss, damage or injury of any kind suffered by another person because ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          113 the first-mentioned person complains about an action under section 70.  (2) Subsection (1) only applies if the complaint is made in good faith."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "41d22277acbe96d50d76a2033b297c6738ae1c836d54327ce3bb16e351df9791" ;
