concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-89h a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "89H Complaints to Ombudsman—certain rights not affected by"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-89h ;
    values:originalText "certificates  (1) This section applies if:  (a) the Ombudsman has commenced an investigation of a decision made under this Act not to grant a request for access to a document; and  (b) the Attorney-General furnishes a certificate to the Ombudsman under paragraph 9(3)(a), (c) or (d) of the Ombudsman Act 1976 in relation to that investigation.  (2) The certificate does not affect the Ombudsman’s right to:  (a) seek from any person the reasons for a decision made under this Act not to give access to an exempt document; or  (b) require any person to give any information or to answer any questions concerning the decision. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments" ;
    skos:definition "certificates  (1) This section applies if:  (a) the Ombudsman has commenced an investigation of a decision made under this Act not to grant a request for access to a document; and  (b) the Attorney-General furnishes a certificate to the Ombudsman under paragraph 9(3)(a), (c) or (d) of the Ombudsman Act 1976 in relation to that investigation.  (2) The certificate does not affect the Ombudsman’s right to:  (a) seek from any person the reasons for a decision made under this Act not to give access to an exempt document; or  (b) require any person to give any information or to answer any questions concerning the decision. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Schedule 4  Information Commissioner amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f78c06aa55a0e2d18b5653884184079a5e77f231af10d7cbdc121b5cb40ef187" ;
    cof:pageNumber "117"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-89h-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-89h-ss-2 ;
