concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-92-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "92 Protection against criminal liability"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-92-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A Minister, or an officer of an agency, is not guilty of a criminal offence only because the Minister or officer:  (a) publishes a document in good faith, in the belief that the publication is required or permitted under Part II (information publication scheme) or section 11C (publication of information in accessed documents); or  (b) gives access to a document in good faith, in the belief that the access is required or permitted to be given in response to a request; or  (c) publishes, or gives access to, a document in good faith, in the belief that the publication or access is required or permitted otherwise than under this Act (whether or not under an express legislative power).  (2) A person is not guilty of a criminal offence only because the person shows a document, or is concerned in the showing of a document, to another person or organisation for any of the following purposes: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          119  (a) consultation with a State under subsection 26A(2);  (b) enabling the other person or the organisation to make a submission under subsection 27(4);  (c) enabling the other person to make a submission under subsection 27A(3)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A Minister, or an officer of an agency, is not guilty of a criminal offence only because the Minister or officer:  (a) publishes a document in good faith, in the belief that the publication is required or permitted under Part II (information publication scheme) or section 11C (publication of information in accessed documents); or  (b) gives access to a document in good faith, in the belief that the access is required or permitted to be given in response to a request; or  (c) publishes, or gives access to, a document in good faith, in the belief that the publication or access is required or permitted otherwise than under this Act (whether or not under an express legislative power).  (2) A person is not guilty of a criminal offence only because the person shows a document, or is concerned in the showing of a document, to another person or organisation for any of the following purposes: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          119  (a) consultation with a State under subsection 26A(2);  (b) enabling the other person or the organisation to make a submission under subsection 27(4);  (c) enabling the other person to make a submission under subsection 27A(3)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2105bdc684a324071d54d3075b4fd4913ee73a98af8035471f17fdc377240c01" ;
    cof:pageNumber "122"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-92-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-92-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf, p.122" .
doc:sch-4-sec-92-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "92 Protection against criminal liability" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A Minister, or an officer of an agency, is not guilty of a criminal offence only because the Minister or officer:  (a) publishes a document in good faith, in the belief that the publication is required or permitted under Part II (information publication scheme) or section 11C (publication of information in accessed documents); or  (b) gives access to a document in good faith, in the belief that the access is required or permitted to be given in response to a request; or  (c) publishes, or gives access to, a document in good faith, in the belief that the publication or access is required or permitted otherwise than under this Act (whether or not under an express legislative power).  (2) A person is not guilty of a criminal offence only because the person shows a document, or is concerned in the showing of a document, to another person or organisation for any of the following purposes: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Information Commissioner amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          119  (a) consultation with a State under subsection 26A(2);  (b) enabling the other person or the organisation to make a submission under subsection 27(4);  (c) enabling the other person to make a submission under subsection 27A(3)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "122"^^xsd:integer .

