concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-4-sec-93 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "93 Agencies to provide information to Information Commissioner"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-93 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies to:  (a) an agency, in relation to documents of the agency; and  (b) each Minister, in relation to his or her official documents.  (2) The agency or Minister must give to the Information Commissioner the information that the Information Commissioner requires to prepare reports under section 30 of the Australian Information Commissioner Act 2010.  (3) The agency or Minister must comply with any requirements prescribed by the regulations regarding:  (a) the giving of the information; and  (b) the keeping of records for the purposes of this section." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies to:  (a) an agency, in relation to documents of the agency; and  (b) each Minister, in relation to his or her official documents.  (2) The agency or Minister must give to the Information Commissioner the information that the Information Commissioner requires to prepare reports under section 30 of the Australian Information Commissioner Act 2010.  (3) The agency or Minister must comply with any requirements prescribed by the regulations regarding:  (a) the giving of the information; and  (b) the keeping of records for the purposes of this section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7fc6a0bc61b47a049cff2cd29565d1d06ead0b35e7f1b7cbbb6998782364e00c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "123"^^xsd:integer ;
