concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-5-sec-12-2-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12(5) Guidelines relating to privacy"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-12-2-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) After the 3-year period ending on 30 June 1998, and after each successive 3-year period, each agency must give the Minister responsible for the agency a report for presentation to the Parliament including all the details relating to the data-matching program carried out during the period that are specified for the purposes of this subsection in guidelines issued under this section. Note: Section 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 sets time limits for giving reports to Ministers and for presentation of reports to the Parliament." ;
    skos:definition "(5) After the 3-year period ending on 30 June 1998, and after each successive 3-year period, each agency must give the Minister responsible for the agency a report for presentation to the Parliament including all the details relating to the data-matching program carried out during the period that are specified for the purposes of this subsection in guidelines issued under this section. Note: Section 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 sets time limits for giving reports to Ministers and for presentation of reports to the Parliament."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5462dff5e103a38d05796ff31cc8bab0689474af8a3dd9b44f624574b52af241" ;
    values:partOf concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-5-sec-12-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "132"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Agency must provide report to Minister on data-matching program." ;
