concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-6-sec-12 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12 Subsection 4(1) (paragraphs (b) and (c) of the definition of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-12 ;
    values:originalText "principal officer) Repeal the paragraphs, substitute:  (b) in relation to a prescribed authority:  (i) if the regulations declare an office to be the principal office of the authority—the person holding, or performing the duties of, that office;  (ii) if the authority is an Agency (within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999) other than a Department and subparagraph (i) does not apply—the Agency Head (within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999) of the authority;  (iii) if neither subparagraph (i) nor (ii) applies—the person responsible for the day-to-day management of the authority;  (iv) if the authority is constituted by one person and none of subparagraphs (i) to (iii) applies—that person;  (v) if the authority is constituted by 2 or more persons and none of subparagraphs (i) to (iv) applies—the person who is entitled to preside at any meeting of the authority at which he or she is present." ;
    skos:definition "principal officer) Repeal the paragraphs, substitute:  (b) in relation to a prescribed authority:  (i) if the regulations declare an office to be the principal office of the authority—the person holding, or performing the duties of, that office;  (ii) if the authority is an Agency (within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999) other than a Department and subparagraph (i) does not apply—the Agency Head (within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999) of the authority;  (iii) if neither subparagraph (i) nor (ii) applies—the person responsible for the day-to-day management of the authority;  (iv) if the authority is constituted by one person and none of subparagraphs (i) to (iii) applies—that person;  (v) if the authority is constituted by 2 or more persons and none of subparagraphs (i) to (iv) applies—the person who is entitled to preside at any meeting of the authority at which he or she is present."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6d7c8aa56b66b9f92297872dede7d18038fd6f4268010f1f4862352aee84f5ac" ;
    cof:pageNumber "142"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines who holds or performs duties in a prescribed authority" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf, p.142" ;
