concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-6-sec-29 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29 At the end of section 15"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-29 ;
    values:originalText "Add: Extension of processing period to consult foreign entity  (7) Subsection (8) applies if, in relation to a request, the agency or Minister determines in writing that it is appropriate to extend the period referred to in paragraph (5)(b) so that the agency or Minister can:  (a) consult one of the following:  (i) a foreign government;  (ii) an authority of a foreign government;  (iii) an international organisation; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Other amendments  Schedule 6 Amendments to the Freedom of Information Act 1982  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          143  (b) determine whether the document that is the subject of the request is an exempt document under subparagraph 33(a)(iii) or paragraph 33(b).  (8) If this subsection applies:  (a) the period referred to in paragraph (5)(b) is extended by a period of 30 days; and  (b) the agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, inform the applicant that the period has been extended." ;
    skos:definition "Add: Extension of processing period to consult foreign entity  (7) Subsection (8) applies if, in relation to a request, the agency or Minister determines in writing that it is appropriate to extend the period referred to in paragraph (5)(b) so that the agency or Minister can:  (a) consult one of the following:  (i) a foreign government;  (ii) an authority of a foreign government;  (iii) an international organisation; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Other amendments  Schedule 6 Amendments to the Freedom of Information Act 1982  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          143  (b) determine whether the document that is the subject of the request is an exempt document under subparagraph 33(a)(iii) or paragraph 33(b).  (8) If this subsection applies:  (a) the period referred to in paragraph (5)(b) is extended by a period of 30 days; and  (b) the agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, inform the applicant that the period has been extended."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bcf57461ee87e8ec58ceb57132a9eec9f1cb9f5d5267a222f5220bb8775c0b25" ;
    cof:pageNumber "146"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-6-sec-29-ss-7 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-6-sec-29-ss-8 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010.pdf, p.146" .
doc:sch-6-sec-29 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "29 At the end of section 15" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Add: Extension of processing period to consult foreign entity  (7) Subsection (8) applies if, in relation to a request, the agency or Minister determines in writing that it is appropriate to extend the period referred to in paragraph (5)(b) so that the agency or Minister can:  (a) consult one of the following:  (i) a foreign government;  (ii) an authority of a foreign government;  (iii) an international organisation; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Other amendments  Schedule 6 Amendments to the Freedom of Information Act 1982  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          143  (b) determine whether the document that is the subject of the request is an exempt document under subparagraph 33(a)(iii) or paragraph 33(b).  (8) If this subsection applies:  (a) the period referred to in paragraph (5)(b) is extended by a period of 30 days; and  (b) the agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, inform the applicant that the period has been extended." ;
    cof:pageNumber "146"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-6-sec-29-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29(7) At the end of section 15"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-29-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) Subsection (8) applies if, in relation to a request, the agency or Minister determines in writing that it is appropriate to extend the period referred to in paragraph (5)(b) so that the agency or Minister can:  (a) consult one of the following:  (i) a foreign government;  (ii) an authority of a foreign government;  (iii) an international organisation; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Other amendments  Schedule 6 Amendments to the Freedom of Information Act 1982  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          143  (b) determine whether the document that is the subject of the request is an exempt document under subparagraph 33(a)(iii) or paragraph 33(b)." ;
    skos:definition "(7) Subsection (8) applies if, in relation to a request, the agency or Minister determines in writing that it is appropriate to extend the period referred to in paragraph (5)(b) so that the agency or Minister can:  (a) consult one of the following:  (i) a foreign government;  (ii) an authority of a foreign government;  (iii) an international organisation; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Other amendments  Schedule 6 Amendments to the Freedom of Information Act 1982  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          143  (b) determine whether the document that is the subject of the request is an exempt document under subparagraph 33(a)(iii) or paragraph 33(b)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b84554372de43fb0cf8022b4ac22d5764746d158b802458787aa3dd206ba17ba" ;
    values:partOf concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-6-sec-29 ;
    cof:pageNumber "146"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Agency or Minister may extend period for request if appropriate to consult foreign government, authority, or international organisation." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
