doc:sch-6-sec-29-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "29(7) At the end of section 15" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) Subsection (8) applies if, in relation to a request, the agency or Minister determines in writing that it is appropriate to extend the period referred to in paragraph (5)(b) so that the agency or Minister can:  (a) consult one of the following:  (i) a foreign government;  (ii) an authority of a foreign government;  (iii) an international organisation; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Other amendments  Schedule 6 Amendments to the Freedom of Information Act 1982  Part 1  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          143  (b) determine whether the document that is the subject of the request is an exempt document under subparagraph 33(a)(iii) or paragraph 33(b)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "146"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-6-sec-29-ss-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29(8) At the end of section 15"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-29-ss-8 ;
    values:originalText "(8) If this subsection applies:  (a) the period referred to in paragraph (5)(b) is extended by a period of 30 days; and  (b) the agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, inform the applicant that the period has been extended." ;
    skos:definition "(8) If this subsection applies:  (a) the period referred to in paragraph (5)(b) is extended by a period of 30 days; and  (b) the agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, inform the applicant that the period has been extended."@en ;
