concept:freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-7-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Review of adjudicator’s decisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-7-sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This item applies if:  (a) a person applied under section 18BI of the Privacy Act 1988 to the Privacy Commissioner for review of a determination made by an adjudicator; and  (b) the Privacy Commissioner did not complete the review before the commencement day. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Privacy Commissioner transition  Schedule 7 Legal and other proceedings  Part 6  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          167 (2) The Information Commissioner may complete the review in accordance with section 18BI of the Privacy Act 1988 on and after the commencement day." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This item applies if:  (a) a person applied under section 18BI of the Privacy Act 1988 to the Privacy Commissioner for review of a determination made by an adjudicator; and  (b) the Privacy Commissioner did not complete the review before the commencement day. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00866  Privacy Commissioner transition  Schedule 7 Legal and other proceedings  Part 6  Freedom of Information Amendment (Reform) Act 2010          167 (2) The Information Commissioner may complete the review in accordance with section 18BI of the Privacy Act 1988 on and after the commencement day."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "911e5520ec1ebb51a34060a5c0d67e25e198709e90e9e567360572826b85ee5c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "170"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Privacy Commissioner must complete a review of an adjudicator's decision if the review was not completed before the commencement day." ;
